---
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="PhD Research Proposal | Daniele Sala"
	description="PhD project plan: Monitoring and Predicting Droughts on National Scale — a satellite-integrated, groundwater-coupled hybrid modelling framework for Denmark. DREAM Programme, Aalborg University."
>
	<div class="stack gap-20">
		<main class="wrapper stack gap-10">
			<Hero
				title="PhD Research Proposal"
				tagline="Monitoring and Predicting Droughts on National Scale: A Satellite-Integrated, Groundwater-Coupled Hybrid Modelling Framework for Denmark"
				align="start"
			/>

			<div class="meta-bar">
				<span class="meta-item"><strong>Programme:</strong> DREAM PhD · Aalborg University</span>
				<span class="meta-item"><strong>Duration:</strong> 36 months</span>
				<span class="meta-item"><strong>Date:</strong> May 2026</span>
				<a href="/docs/research-proposal.pdf" target="_blank" class="meta-download">
					<Icon icon="arrow-right" size="1em" /> Download PDF
				</a>
			</div>

			<div class="proposal-content">

				<!-- ABSTRACT -->
				<section class="abstract-box">
					<p>
						The PhD will deliver a satellite-fed VIC Denmark system producing a probabilistic
						four-pillar combined drought index and short- to seasonal-scale predictions of water
						dynamics. It closes a structural gap in Denmark's drought early warning landscape by
						coupling groundwater state to a national-scale land surface model and integrating
						multi-source satellite observations via ensemble data assimilation.
					</p>
				</section>

				<!-- PROBLEM STATEMENT -->
				<section>
					<h2>1. Problem Statement and Motivation</h2>
					<p>
						The 2018 Danish drought caused agricultural losses exceeding <strong>DKK 6 billion</strong>
						and exposed a structural gap in the national early warning landscape. Operational systems
						such as <strong>HIP</strong> and the <strong>DK model</strong> deliver high-resolution
						diagnostics but lack probabilistic, satellite-integrated outlooks at sub-seasonal to
						seasonal lead times.
					</p>
					<p>
						Meanwhile, macro-scale land surface models such as <strong>VIC</strong> — the model
						targeted by the DREAM call — lack a prognostic groundwater state. In a country where
						more than 99% of drinking water originates from aquifers, where water tables typically
						lie 1–5 metres below surface, and where more than half of the agricultural area is
						sub-surface drained, this gap is a first-order limitation.
					</p>
					<p>
						Forootan et al. (2024) showed that the severity of the 2017–2021 European drought is
						systematically underestimated in non-assimilated W3RA — confirming that closing this
						loop through groundwater coupling, multi-source data assimilation, and hybrid
						physics/ML integration is both timely and necessary.
					</p>
				</section>

				<!-- RESEARCH QUESTIONS -->
				<section>
					<h2>2. Research Questions</h2>
					<div class="rq-grid">
						<div class="rq-card">
							<span class="rq-label">RQ1</span>
							<p>
								Can a groundwater-coupled VIC Denmark, constrained by joint assimilation of
								<strong>GRACE FO</strong> terrestrial water storage, <strong>SMAP</strong> and
								<strong>ESA CCI</strong> soil moisture, streamflow, and Jupiter piezometric heads,
								reproduce the propagation of meteorological, agricultural, hydrological, and
								groundwater drought signals better than uncoupled or non-assimilated baselines?
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="rq-card">
							<span class="rq-label">RQ2</span>
							<p>
								Does a hybrid framework combining differentiable parameter learning with LSTM
								post-processing trained on <strong>CAMELS DK</strong> recover predictive skill
								in groundwater-dominated Danish catchments, where pure LSTMs underperform
								(Liu et al. 2024)?
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="rq-card">
							<span class="rq-label">RQ3</span>
							<p>
								Can a probabilistic four-pillar combined index (SPI/SPEI + SSMI + SSI + SGI),
								aggregated via copulas, classify drought severity more skilfully than
								<strong>EDO CDI v4</strong> and improve seasonal predictability when forced with
								<strong>SEAS5</strong> and <strong>AIFS ENS</strong> or GenCast?
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</section>

				<!-- WORK PACKAGES -->
				<section>
					<h2>3. Work Packages</h2>
					<div class="wp-list">
						<div class="wp-item">
							<div class="wp-header">
								<span class="wp-badge">WP1</span>
								<h3>VIC Denmark with Groundwater Coupling</h3>
							</div>
							<p>
								National VIC 5 at 1–10 km, parameterised from VICGlobal and refined with Danish
								hydrostratigraphy from GEUS and Jupiter wells. The groundwater module follows
								<strong>SIMGM</strong> (Niu et al. 2007), with a staged escalation path to 2D
								lateral coupling if validation justifies it.
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="wp-item">
							<div class="wp-header">
								<span class="wp-badge">WP2</span>
								<h3>Joint Calibration and Multi-Source Data Assimilation</h3>
							</div>
							<p>
								<strong>LETKF</strong> and <strong>ConBay</strong> MCMC assimilating GRACE FO
								terrestrial water storage (sub-monthly L1B), SMAP and ESA CCI soil moisture,
								streamflow, and Jupiter piezometric heads. Built on <strong>PyGLDA</strong>
								(Yang et al. 2025) with Fennoscandian GIA correction via ICE-6G_D.
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="wp-item">
							<div class="wp-header">
								<span class="wp-badge">WP3</span>
								<h3>Hybrid Extension via Differentiable Hydrology</h3>
							</div>
							<p>
								Differentiable VIC trained via <strong>dPL</strong> (Tsai et al. 2021) on
								CAMELS DK across 3,330 basins — replacing per-basin calibration with
								gradient-based learning. An LSTM residual post-processor corrects biases in
								groundwater-dominated catchments.
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="wp-item">
							<div class="wp-header">
								<span class="wp-badge">WP4</span>
								<h3>Probabilistic Four-Pillar Drought Index</h3>
							</div>
							<p>
								Standardised sub-indices spanning the full propagation chain —
								SPI/SPEI · SSMI · SSI · SGI — aggregated via copulas into a probabilistic
								<strong>Multi-pillar Combined Drought Index (MCDI)</strong> with full posterior
								probabilities of drought severity categories.
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="wp-item">
							<div class="wp-header">
								<span class="wp-badge">WP5</span>
								<h3>Short- to Seasonal-Scale Forecasting</h3>
							</div>
							<p>
								VIC DK forced with <strong>SEAS5</strong> and <strong>AIFS ENS</strong> or
								GenCast for 1–6 month outlooks, evaluated via CRPS, Brier score, and ROC.
								Benchmarks: EFAS Seasonal and EDgE.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</section>

				<!-- TIMELINE -->
				<section>
					<h2>4. Project Timeline (36 months)</h2>
					<div class="timeline-table">
						<div class="tl-header">
							<span>Work Package</span>
							<span class="tl-yr">Year 1</span>
							<span class="tl-yr">Year 2</span>
							<span class="tl-yr">Year 3</span>
						</div>
						{[
							{ wp: 'WP1: VIC + GW', y1: 100, y2: 30, y3: 0, note: 'Decision point: 2D lateral coupling (month 12)' },
							{ wp: 'WP2: Data Assimilation', y1: 60, y2: 100, y3: 40, note: 'Runs in parallel throughout' },
							{ wp: 'WP3: Hybrid ML', y1: 0, y2: 80, y3: 100, note: 'Milestone: hybrid competence (month 24)' },
							{ wp: 'WP4: MCDI', y1: 0, y2: 60, y3: 100, note: 'Copula aggregation in Year 2–3' },
							{ wp: 'WP5: Forecasting', y1: 0, y2: 20, y3: 100, note: 'Milestone: operational prototype (month 36)' },
						].map(({ wp, y1, y2, y3, note }) => (
							<div class="tl-row">
								<span class="tl-label">{wp}</span>
								<div class="tl-bar-cell">
									<div class="tl-bar" style={`width: ${y1}%`}></div>
								</div>
								<div class="tl-bar-cell">
									<div class="tl-bar" style={`width: ${y2}%`}></div>
								</div>
								<div class="tl-bar-cell">
									<div class="tl-bar" style={`width: ${y3}%`}></div>
								</div>
							</div>
						))}
					</div>
				</section>

				<!-- CHALLENGES -->
				<section>
					<h2>5. Expected Challenges and Mitigations</h2>
					<div class="challenge-grid">
						<div class="challenge-card">
							<h3>Scale Mismatch</h3>
							<p class="challenge-desc">GRACE FO ~300 km resolution vs Denmark's 43,000 km²</p>
							<p>Sub-monthly L1B assimilation · ConBay merging with SMAP · ML-based downscaling against Jupiter wells · GIA correction via ICE-6G_D</p>
						</div>
						<div class="challenge-card">
							<h3>Equifinality</h3>
							<p class="challenge-desc">Multiple parameter sets can reproduce equivalent streamflow with incorrect subsurface partitioning</p>
							<p>GEUS-derived priors on aquifer parameters · LETKF localisation and inflation · dPL as deterministic precursor before stochastic assimilation</p>
						</div>
						<div class="challenge-card">
							<h3>ML Physical Consistency</h3>
							<p class="challenge-desc">Pure LSTMs may extrapolate poorly and do not guarantee mass conservation</p>
							<p>VIC as physical backbone · LSTM restricted to residual post-processor role · Conformal prediction for honest uncertainty intervals</p>
						</div>
						<div class="challenge-card">
							<h3>Index Collapse</h3>
							<p class="challenge-desc">Naive averaging of indices with different time scales loses causal propagation and tail dependence</p>
							<p>Pillar-appropriate scales (SPI 1–3 months, SGI 6–12 months) · Copula aggregation preserving tail dependence · Validation against Naturskaderådet claims and crop yield anomalies</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</section>

				<!-- EXPECTED OUTPUTS -->
				<section>
					<h2>6. Expected Outputs</h2>
					<ul class="outputs-list">
						<li>Three first-author papers in <em>Water Resources Research</em>, <em>Hydrology and Earth System Sciences</em>, and <em>Remote Sensing of Environment</em> or <em>Science of The Total Environment</em></li>
						<li>An open-source VIC DK + ConBay data assimilation codebase released through PyGLDA</li>
						<li>An operational MCDI prototype co-designed with DMI, GEUS, and Naturskaderådet end-users</li>
					</ul>
				</section>

				<!-- BACKGROUND -->
				<section>
					<h2>7. Background and Added Value</h2>
					<p>
						My M.Sc. thesis at Politecnico di Milano — building, calibrating, and running sensitivity
						and uncertainty analysis on the FEST process-based hydrological model over the Po basin —
						gave me direct experience of the central methodological tension this project addresses:
						constraining subsurface parameters from surface observations alone.
					</p>
					<p>
						My current operational role at Progesi S.p.A., running multi-hazard monitoring with ICON
						and ECMWF IFS forcing, satellite-derived diagnostics, and Python/R/MATLAB workflows for
						Regione Lombardia, translates directly to the operational demands of a national-scale
						drought early warning system.
					</p>
					<p>
						This combination of process-based modelling, applied data science, and operational
						hydrometeorology positions me to contribute to WP1 and WP2 immediately, while developing
						the hybrid ML competence for WP3 through structured upskilling in NeuralHydrology,
						PyTorch, and differentiable hydrology.
					</p>
				</section>

				<div class="pdf-cta">
					<CallToAction href="/docs/research-proposal.pdf">
						Download Full Proposal (PDF)
						<Icon icon="arrow-right" size="1.2em" />
					</CallToAction>
				</div>

			</div>
		</main>

		<ContactCTA />
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.meta-bar {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 1rem 2rem;
		align-items: center;
		padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
		background: var(--gray-999_40);
		border: 1px solid var(--gray-800);
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--gray-300);
	}

	.meta-download {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.3em;
		color: var(--accent-regular);
		text-decoration: none;
		font-weight: 500;
		margin-left: auto;
	}

	.meta-download:hover {
		text-decoration: underline;
	}

	.proposal-content {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 3rem;
	}

	.proposal-content section h2 {
		font-size: var(--text-2xl);
		color: var(--gray-0);
		margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
		padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
		border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent-regular);
	}

	.proposal-content section p {
		color: var(--gray-200);
		line-height: 1.75;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	/* Abstract */
	.abstract-box {
		padding: 1.5rem 2rem;
		background: var(--accent-overlay);
		border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-regular);
		border-radius: 0 0.5rem 0.5rem 0;
	}

	.abstract-box p {
		font-size: var(--text-lg);
		font-style: italic;
		color: var(--gray-100) !important;
		margin: 0 !important;
	}

	/* Research questions */
	.rq-grid {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
	}

	.rq-card {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding: 1.25rem;
		background: var(--gray-999_40);
		border: 1px solid var(--gray-800);
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
	}

	.rq-label {
		font-family: var(--font-brand);
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: var(--text-lg);
		color: var(--accent-regular);
		padding-top: 0.1rem;
	}

	.rq-card p {
		margin: 0 !important;
	}

	/* Work packages */
	.wp-list {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1rem;
	}

	.wp-item {
		padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
		background: var(--gray-999_40);
		border: 1px solid var(--gray-800);
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
		border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-regular);
	}

	.wp-header {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
	}

	.wp-badge {
		font-family: var(--font-brand);
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--accent-text-over);
		background: var(--accent-regular);
		padding: 0.2em 0.6em;
		border-radius: 999rem;
		white-space: nowrap;
	}

	.wp-header h3 {
		font-size: var(--text-lg);
		color: var(--gray-0);
		margin: 0;
	}

	.wp-item p {
		margin: 0 !important;
	}

	/* Timeline */
	.timeline-table {
		border: 1px solid var(--gray-800);
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
		overflow: hidden;
	}

	.tl-header,
	.tl-row {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 14rem 1fr 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 0;
	}

	.tl-header {
		background: var(--gray-900);
		font-family: var(--font-brand);
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--gray-300);
		padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
	}

	.tl-yr {
		text-align: center;
	}

	.tl-row {
		padding: 0.6rem 1rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--gray-800);
		background: var(--gray-999_40);
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.5rem;
	}

	.tl-row:nth-child(even) {
		background: transparent;
	}

	.tl-label {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--gray-200);
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	.tl-bar-cell {
		padding: 0 0.5rem;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
	}

	.tl-bar {
		height: 0.6rem;
		background: var(--gradient-accent-orange);
		border-radius: 999rem;
		min-width: 0;
	}

	/* Challenges */
	.challenge-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 1rem;
	}

	.challenge-card {
		padding: 1.25rem;
		background: var(--gray-999_40);
		border: 1px solid var(--gray-800);
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
	}

	.challenge-card h3 {
		font-size: var(--text-md);
		color: var(--gray-0);
		margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
	}

	.challenge-desc {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--gray-400);
		font-style: italic;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem !important;
	}

	.challenge-card p {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--gray-300);
		margin: 0 !important;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	/* Outputs */
	.outputs-list {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.outputs-list li {
		padding-left: 1.5rem;
		position: relative;
		color: var(--gray-200);
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	.outputs-list li::before {
		content: '▸';
		position: absolute;
		left: 0;
		color: var(--accent-regular);
	}

	.pdf-cta {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: flex-start;
		padding-top: 1rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 50em) {
		.challenge-grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}

		.tl-header,
		.tl-row {
			grid-template-columns: 9rem 1fr 1fr 1fr;
		}

		.meta-download {
			margin-left: 0;
		}
	}
</style>
